# Forward PWAs still re-fetching the old hashed manifest URL (now gone)
# to the stable path. `_redirects` fire even when no asset matches.
# Removable in ~a month, once most installs have refreshed.
#
# Anchor the match to the `.webmanifest` extension: a bare `manifest-*`
# splat also swallows hashed route chunks like `manifest-route-<hash>.js`
# (301'd to JSON, they break the gallery's dynamic import). The `:hash`
# placeholder matches any non-`/` run — hyphenated hashes included — while
# the trailing literal keeps it scoped to the old manifest asset.
/_build/assets/manifest-:hash.webmanifest  /manifest.webmanifest  301

# The icon editor moved to its own worker. Forward old links there; the query
# string carries the editor state (`?icon=…`) and passes through untouched.
# Prod-only: `_redirects` can't match or rewrite by host, so previews and
# staging forward to prod too. The bare path needs its own rule: the splat
# doesn't match `/icon-editor` without a trailing slash.
/icon-editor    https://icon-editor.psychollama.io/        301
/icon-editor/*  https://icon-editor.psychollama.io/:splat  301

# The gallery moved to its own worker, with manifest pages at the root
# (`/gallery/lib-ui` → `/lib-ui`). Prod-only for the same reason as above.
/gallery    https://gallery.psychollama.io/        301
/gallery/*  https://gallery.psychollama.io/:splat  301

# The QR reader moved to its own worker, served from the root. Prod-only for
# the same reason as above.
/scanner    https://qr.psychollama.io/        301
/scanner/*  https://qr.psychollama.io/:splat  301

# Beam moved to its own worker, served from the root. Old invite links
# (`/beam/share/<id>`) land on `/share/<id>` there. Prod-only for the same
# reason as above.
/beam    https://beam.psychollama.io/        301
/beam/*  https://beam.psychollama.io/:splat  301
